MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The external hard drive feels useful for storing files and backups alongside the computer equipment I use, though 12TB may be more capacity than I need.",
    "The HDMI cable and cable modem connect with my interest in practical connectivity, reflected in my HDMI cable, Ethernet adapter and Ethernet cable purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo devices and Fire streaming devices introduce voice-assistant and entertainment uses that do not address my current computer maintenance and connectivity needs.",
    "Specific connections matter: buying headphones does not mean I need optical audio, and buying an HDMI cable does not mean I need to mirror a source onto two displays."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations treat an interest in electronics as a reason to want smart speakers, tablets and streaming devices, even though those serve different purposes from my recent purchases.",
    "My Amazon Basics accessories and Kindle seem to have been taken as broader interest in Amazon devices, when their practical uses matter more to me than their brand."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet accessories, headphone mount and blower duster point toward connecting, organizing and maintaining an existing computer setup.",
    "Relevance does not always create a purchase need: I already bought an HDMI cable, and I would need to confirm service compatibility and a reason to replace my modem before choosing another one."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my interest in useful computer equipment but stretch it too far into general electronics without enough attention to the task each purchase serves."
}
